# 3.3. Standard Notations and Common Functions

This is the canonical fourth-edition reader facade for the standard functions
used throughout CLRS.  The imported theorem modules cover integer rounding,
modular arithmetic, exponentials and logarithms, factorials, functional
iteration, Fibonacci numbers, and the growth hierarchy.

## Main results

The page exposes the proved floor, ceiling, remainder, logarithm, factorial,
iteration, and Fibonacci identities; real-exponent and polynomial-growth
bridges; the hierarchy through {lit}`n^(log n)` and {lit}`n^n`; and the exact
effective Robbins refinement of Stirling's formula.

Status: `proved` for the represented identities and growth comparisons.
